WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.119
The prize photograph records a few names. The

00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:07.329
publications behind it often record many hands,

00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:08.705
instruments and years.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.977
The prize ceremony produces a clear picture of

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:22.946
discovery, with a handful of faces attached to a

00:00:22.946 --> 00:00:24.269
complicated scientific history.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.458
Experiments accumulate through earlier questions,

00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:37.466
technical adaptations, overlooked collaborators and

00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:41.678
results that sometimes become useful years later.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.038
A manuscript records coauthors, while a method may

00:00:50.038 --> 00:00:53.177
depend on technicians, students and predecessor teams

00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:55.419
who never enter the headline.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.769
Every selection tells us whom an institution has chosen

00:01:05.769 --> 00:01:09.129
to remember. Historical recognition is never identical

00:01:09.129 --> 00:01:12.008
to an exhaustive chain of contribution.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.033
Recognising overlooked labour does not erase a decisive

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:25.512
insight; it asks us to document how that insight became

00:01:25.512 --> 00:01:25.960
possible.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.490
An inclusive account cannot simply invent forgotten

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.964
heroes. It must return to papers, notebooks, patents

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.570
and who actually did the work.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.824
Discovery can be celebrated without making its history

00:01:49.824 --> 00:01:51.932
smaller than it actually was.
